# Stage-4 cluster tier (amendments C4, C5 of 2026-10-27) of native_transport_max_concurrent_connections-channelActive-limit--autonomous.
# Observe-only rules; output goes to the node's stdout. (NTCMEM rule adapted from
# harness/native_transport_max_concurrent_connections_per_ip-channelActive-perIpLimit--autonomous/ntpip.btm.)

# C5: one line per refused channel, at the first ChannelHandlerContext.close() call in channelActive, which is the global-limit
# branch (ConnectionLimitHandler.java:97); the per-IP branch is not reached with the per-IP limit off.
RULE ntc refuse at global close
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.transport.ConnectionLimitHandler
METHOD channelActive
AT INVOKE io.netty.channel.ChannelHandlerContext.close
IF true
DO traceln("NTCREFUSE t=" + System.currentTimeMillis() + " counter=" + $0.counter.get() + " limit=" + org.apache.cassandra.config.DatabaseDescriptor.getNativeTransportMaxConcurrentConnections())
ENDRULE

# C4: the native-transport allocator's metric (capacity bytes of its live direct and heap buffers) and the handler's counter,
# printed on every `nodetool version` call (StorageService.getReleaseVersion). The binding needs the heap-allocator flag
# (CBUtil.allocator is then an UnpooledByteBufAllocator).

RULE ntc allocator metric on nodetool version
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.service.StorageService
METHOD getReleaseVersion
AT ENTRY
BIND a : io.netty.buffer.UnpooledByteBufAllocator = org.apache.cassandra.transport.CBUtil.allocator;
     m : io.netty.buffer.ByteBufAllocatorMetric = a.metric();
     h = org.apache.cassandra.transport.PipelineConfigurator.connectionLimitHandler
IF true
DO traceln("NTCMEM t=" + System.currentTimeMillis() + " direct=" + m.usedDirectMemory() + " heap=" + m.usedHeapMemory() + " allocator=" + org.apache.cassandra.transport.CBUtil.allocator.getClass().getSimpleName() + " heapAllocatorFlag=" + org.apache.cassandra.transport.CBUtil.USE_HEAP_ALLOCATOR + " counter=" + h.counter.get())
ENDRULE
